# ── Line endings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source is LF, in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this an editor or script on Windows can save a file back as CRLF, which turns a one-line
# change into a whole-file diff and buries the actual edit. That happened to
# src/lib/stats/rankings-columns.ts on 2026-08-31: a four-line change arrived as 2,405.
*.ts     text eol=lf
*.tsx    text eol=lf
*.mts    text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.jsx    text eol=lf
*.css    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.sql    text eol=lf
*.prisma text eol=lf

# ── Captured data is not source ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The archive is scraped Wayback material and the verification fixtures are recorded output. Both
# are evidence of what something WAS, so they are left byte-for-byte as captured rather than
# rewritten to match a house style they were never written in.
archive/**              -text
verification/**         -text
deploy-artifacts/**     -text
